        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12327828/comment/12363235",
          "id": "12363235",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stefan%40jira",
            "name": "stefan@jira",
            "key": "stefan@jira",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stefan Guggisberg",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "note that allowing an application to dynamically modify the configuration \n*after* the repository has been initialized may lead to unexpected results.\n\njackrabbit's code expects the configuration to be immutable. public access \nmodifyers and setters have been intentionally omitted for this reason.\n\nif those are to be made public the documentation has to clearly and explicitly \nmention the danger of dynamically changing the configuration.\n\npersonally i'd prefer a tool where a config xml file/dom tree could be easily built \nprogrammatically rather than messing around with the live config.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stefan%40jira",
            "name": "stefan@jira",
            "key": "stefan@jira",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stefan Guggisberg",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2006-01-19T20:11:10.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-01-19T20:11:10.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12327828/comment/12363253",
          "id": "12363253",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636"
            },
            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "body": "i strongly oppose to apply the suggested patch. stefan is right - the internals of jackrabbit rely on the fact that the config classes are immutable. we should not break this.\n\ni suggest to create some sort of ConfigBuilder which has all the relevant getter and setter methods, and a 'create()' method that creates the immutable config objects.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
